{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00752",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 0.63,
      "end_seconds": 12.78,
      "duration_seconds": 12.15,
      "text": "Morning, doctor! I'm Donna, I'm Leo's foster carer, we've had him eight months. He's two and a half, and I'm worried because he's not talking."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 14.61,
      "end_seconds": 21.28,
      "duration_seconds": 6.67,
      "text": "Hello Donna, hello Leo. Leo, what have you got there? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 23.82,
      "end_seconds": 25.36,
      "duration_seconds": 1.54,
      "text": "Car. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 28.28,
      "end_seconds": 32.54,
      "duration_seconds": 4.26,
      "text": "A car! Does it go fast? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 33.63,
      "end_seconds": 35.44,
      "duration_seconds": 1.81,
      "text": "Brum. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 38.33,
      "end_seconds": 47.92,
      "duration_seconds": 9.59,
      "text": "That's about it, doctor. He says car, brum, no, and mama, which he says to everyone. Not much else."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 50.82,
      "end_seconds": 57.07,
      "duration_seconds": 6.25,
      "text": "Does he put two words together, like 'more juice' or 'big car'?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 58.06,
      "end_seconds": 64.59,
      "duration_seconds": 6.53,
      "text": "Never. He points, and grunts, and gets frustrated and throws things."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 66.1,
      "end_seconds": 72.3,
      "duration_seconds": 6.2,
      "text": "Does he follow instructions, like 'give me the ball' or 'where's your shoe'?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 74.09,
      "end_seconds": 82.05,
      "duration_seconds": 7.96,
      "text": "Sometimes. If you show him. If you just say it, he doesn't always seem to understand."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 84.73,
      "end_seconds": 91.55,
      "duration_seconds": 6.82,
      "text": "Has he had a hearing test, or lots of ear infections?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 93.11,
      "end_seconds": 103.07,
      "duration_seconds": 9.96,
      "text": "He had loads of ear infections before he came to me, and grommets put in at eighteen months."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 104.1,
      "end_seconds": 111.19,
      "duration_seconds": 7.09,
      "text": "Any other medical history, or anything about his birth I should know?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 113.2,
      "end_seconds": 119.99,
      "duration_seconds": 6.79,
      "text": "He was born early, at thirty-two weeks. That's in his notes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 120.82,
      "end_seconds": 123.8,
      "duration_seconds": 2.98,
      "text": "Is he on any medicines?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 125.95,
      "end_seconds": 131.8,
      "duration_seconds": 5.85,
      "text": "Vitamin D drops, once a day. I give them every morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 134.6,
      "end_seconds": 136.17,
      "duration_seconds": 1.57,
      "text": "Mama. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 137.74,
      "end_seconds": 149.42,
      "duration_seconds": 11.68,
      "text": "Hmm, I'm not sure I give them every day, if I'm honest. When it's chaos in the morning, I forget."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 152.12,
      "end_seconds": 164.4,
      "duration_seconds": 12.28,
      "text": "That's very normal. I'll note that they're meant to be daily and that some days are missed. Does he go to nursery, or have other children around?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 166.24,
      "end_seconds": 171.92,
      "duration_seconds": 5.68,
      "text": "Nursery three days a week, and his foster brother is five."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 172.94,
      "end_seconds": 178.25,
      "duration_seconds": 5.31,
      "text": "Does he make eye contact and play with others? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 180.82,
      "end_seconds": 190.44,
      "duration_seconds": 9.62,
      "text": "Yes, he loves cuddles, he waves bye-bye, he plays peekaboo. He's a very sociable boy. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 192.67,
      "end_seconds": 205.75,
      "duration_seconds": 13.08,
      "text": "That's reassuring, because those are good signs for social development. Let me examine him. Leo, can I look in your ears? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 208.44,
      "end_seconds": 209.89,
      "duration_seconds": 1.45,
      "text": "No. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 228.62,
      "end_seconds": 233.55,
      "duration_seconds": 4.93,
      "text": "Just a quick look, with a torch."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 235.11,
      "end_seconds": 244.57,
      "duration_seconds": 9.46,
      "text": "The grommets are in place, both ears look clean and dry, and I can see no fluid behind the eardrums."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 245.7,
      "end_seconds": 249.43,
      "duration_seconds": 3.73,
      "text": "Is it his hearing, then? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 251.52,
      "end_seconds": 270.33,
      "duration_seconds": 18.81,
      "text": "It might be partly. With his history of ear infections, hearing is the first thing to check. Overall, I think this is speech delay, probably related to the early ear problems and prematurity."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 271.5,
      "end_seconds": 275.31,
      "duration_seconds": 3.81,
      "text": "Will he catch up? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 277.01,
      "end_seconds": 292.4,
      "duration_seconds": 15.39,
      "text": "Many children do, especially with support. I'd like to arrange a hearing test, an audiology assessment, and a referral to the speech and language therapist."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 294.59,
      "end_seconds": 297.89,
      "duration_seconds": 3.3,
      "text": "How long will that take? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 299.55,
      "end_seconds": 314.09,
      "duration_seconds": 14.54,
      "text": "A few weeks for the hearing test. Meanwhile, talk to him constantly, name things, read picture books, and don't finish his sentences for him."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 315.85,
      "end_seconds": 319.88,
      "duration_seconds": 4.03,
      "text": "I do like a book. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 321.03,
      "end_seconds": 334.55,
      "duration_seconds": 13.52,
      "text": "And reduce screen time. If he loses words he already has, or seems not to respond to loud sounds, come back sooner."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 337.02,
      "end_seconds": 341.4,
      "duration_seconds": 4.38,
      "text": "I will. Thank you so much. ~"
    }
  ]
}
